distinguish between the hats and the socks.
The morning of the Hogsmeade visit dawned bright but windy. After
breakfast they queued up in front of Filch, who matched their names to the
long list of students who had permission from their parents or guardian to
visit the village. With a slight pang, Harry remembered that if it hadn’t been
for Sirius, he would not have been going at all.
When Harry reached Filch, the caretaker gave a great sniff as though trying
