“’Night,” grunted Ron, from somewhere to his right.
“’Night,” said Harry.
Maybe next time . . . if there was a next time . . . she’d be a bit happier. He
ought to have asked her out; she had probably been expecting it and was now
really angry with him . . . or was she lying in bed, still crying about Cedric?
