died. Just stop worrying . . .”
He clapped Harry on the shoulder and left the pantry, leaving Harry
standing alone in the dark.
Everyone but Harry spent the rest of the morning sleeping. He went up to the
bedroom he had shared with Ron over the summer, but while Ron crawled
into bed and was asleep within minutes, Harry sat fully clothed, hunched
against the cold metal bars of the bedstead, keeping himself deliberately
uncomfortable, determined not to fall into a doze, terrified that he might
become the serpent again in his sleep and awake to find that he had attacked
Ron, or else slithered through the house after one of the others. . . .
When Ron woke up, Harry pretended to have enjoyed a refreshing nap too.
Their trunks arrived from Hogwarts while they were eating lunch, so that they
could dress as Muggles for the trip to St. Mungo’s. Everybody except Harry
