Mad-Eye growled his approval of this idea and set himself with his back
against the corridor wall, his magical eye spinning in all directions. Harry
drew back too, but Mrs. Weasley reached out a hand and pushed him through
the door, saying, “Don’t be silly, Harry, Arthur wants to thank you . . .”
The ward was small and rather dingy as the only window was narrow and
set high in the wall facing the door. Most of the light came from more shining
