panelled oak and there was a portrait of a rather vicious-looking wizard on the
wall, captioned URQUHART RACKHARROW, 1612–1697, INVENTOR OF THE ENTRAILEXPELLING CURSE.
There were only three patients. Mr. Weasley was occupying the bed at the
far end of the ward beside the tiny window. Harry was pleased and relieved to
see that he was propped up on several pillows and reading the Daily Prophet
by the solitary ray of sunlight falling onto his bed. He looked around as they
walked toward him and, seeing whom it was, beamed.
