He pushed open the kitchen door a minute or two later to find Sirius and
Snape both seated at the long kitchen table, glaring in opposite directions. The
silence between them was heavy with mutual dislike. A letter lay open on the
table in front of Sirius.
“Er,” said Harry to announce his presence.
Snape looked around at him, his face framed between curtains of greasy
black hair.
“Sit down, Potter.”
“You know,” said Sirius loudly, leaning back on his rear chair legs and
