I know you like to feel . . . involved.”
“What’s that supposed to mean?” said Sirius, letting his chair fall back onto
all four legs with a loud bang.
“Merely that I am sure you must feel — ah — frustrated by the fact that
you can do nothing useful,” Snape laid a delicate stress on the word, “for the
Order.”
It was Sirius’s turn to flush. Snape’s lip curled in triumph as he turned to
Harry.
“The headmaster has sent me to tell you, Potter, that it is his wish for you to
