The castle grounds were gleaming in the sunlight as though freshly painted;
the cloudless sky smiled at itself in the smoothly sparkling lake, the satingreen lawns rippled occasionally in a gentle breeze: June had arrived, but to
the fifth years this meant only one thing: Their O.W.L.s were upon them at
last.
Their teachers were no longer setting them homework; lessons were
devoted to reviewing those topics their teachers thought most likely to come
up in the exams. The purposeful, feverish atmosphere drove nearly everything
but the O.W.L.s from Harry’s mind, though he did wonder occasionally
during Potions lessons whether Lupin had ever told Snape that he must
continue giving Harry Occlumency tuition: If he had, then Snape had ignored
