and had not laid out any elf clothes for days.
She was not the only person acting oddly as the O.W.L.s drew steadily
nearer. Ernie Macmillan had developed an irritating habit of interrogating
people about their study habits.
“How many hours d’you think you’re doing a day?” he demanded of Harry
and Ron as they queued outside Herbology, a manic gleam in his eyes.
“I dunno,” said Ron. “A few . . .”
“More or less than eight?”
“Less, I s’pose,” said Ron, looking slightly alarmed.
“I’m doing eight,” said Ernie, puffing out his chest. “Eight or nine. I’m
getting an hour in before breakfast every day. Eight’s my average. I can do ten
