“Harry Potter, Ron Weasley, Hermione Granger,” Harry said very quickly,
“Ginny Weasley, Neville Longbottom, Luna Lovegood . . . We’re here to save
someone, unless your Ministry can do it first!”
“Thank you,” said the cool female voice. “Visitors, please take the badges
and attach them to the front of your robes.”
Half a dozen badges slid out of the metal chute where returned coins
usually appeared. Hermione scooped them up and handed them mutely to
Harry over Ginny’s head; he glanced at the topmost one.
