hold of him, and he couldn’t really think of anything else he would like to be.
Moreover, it had seemed the right destiny for him since he had heard the
prophecy a few weeks ago. . . . Neither can live while the other survives. . . .
Wouldn’t he be living up to the prophecy, and giving himself the best chance
of survival, if he joined those highly trained wizards whose job it was to find
